Job Description:

“BDO Advisory” CJSC is looking for a Business Development Specialist, who will be responsible for acquiring new clients, winning new contracts, and driving the company’s growth serving across both private and public sectors. The BD Officer will manage specific proposals in response to competitive tenders issued by potential client organizations and be responsible for developing responsive, compelling, and high-quality proposals.

Job responsibilities

Proposal Management (40%)

Manage the entire process of developing proposals, ranging from articulating the proposal strategy to producing the final proposal for submission;
Ensure that technical proposals meet client requirements and the Company’s quality standards and clearly communicate the Company’s competitive advantage;
Daily activities include:
Analyze Requests for Proposals (RFPs) and determine compliance with RFP requirements;
Articulate proposal strategy, technical solution, and the Company’s win themes;
Maintain proposal calendars and convene and facilitate kick-off and subsequent proposal meetings;
Organize collaborative proposal reviews;
Collaborate with colleagues to assemble technical inputs and define technical solutions to client requirements;
Collaborate with the Head of Service to prepare proposal budgets.
Work across different tendering platforms (including major international financial corporations’ platforms) for screening, selecting and proposing projects for bidding;
Manage the bidding process till the successful winning of the project.

Customer Service (40%)

Integrate, compile, analyze and evaluate all sources of CRM data including tendering, customer, transactional, engagement and product data and identify key trends;
Provide valuable insights of customer behavior, develop customer activity profiles through statistical analysis;
Identify and define different customer segments and provide insights into efficient targeting, conversion and retaining of customers, monitoring monthly change of user categories;
Develop a holistic view of the customer lifecycle and the impact of implemented CRM strategies throughout the entire lifecycle of the customer;
Conduct business analysis, identify key factors and causation links by evaluating information gathered from multiple sources (including customer surveys) to form a solid understanding of business processes from low-level information and be able to make daily and monthly comparisons;
Manage the CRM software and prepare regular dashboards for monitoring and projects’ assessment purposes.

Other Executive Administrative Matters (20%)

Assist the Head of Advisory Services in executive administrative matters and business development initiatives, including but not limited to:

Organize conferences and roundtable discussions;
Engage in marketing activities, client relations and roadshows;
Engage and lead other business development initiatives both for the brand awareness, as well as for lead generation purposes.
Required qualifications
Degree in Economics, Finance, Business, or other relevant fields;
Proven working experience in business analysis/business development;
Strong analytical mindset;
Excellent English writing and verbal skills;
1-3 years of professional experience;
Experience managing or writing proposals for a management consulting company, an IT Company, a nonprofit, or a similar organization;
Experience in or familiarity with the international financial institutions (preferred);
Advanced skills in Microsoft Office;
A CRM software knowledge and skills will be a plus;
Excellent organizational and interpersonal skills;
Able to operate under pressure, multitask, and meet deadlines;
Strong work ethic and desire to excel and keep growing over time.
