The American University of Armenia (AUA) Extension is the non-degree arm of the University that plays a key role in the education, growth, and advancement of regional communities by providing essential learning and practice opportunities, particularly with training in English language and topical areas most essential to each community. Our overarching goal is to ensure that rural communities have access to the knowledge and skills for the betterment of local residents. AUA Extension is appropriately resourced in various areas of adult learning, including languages, tourism and hospitality, small and medium-sized enterprise (MSME) support, as well as leadership and management, women’s entrepreneurship, information technologies, and other topics that may be most effective to meet the needs of local populations.

