Job Description:

Provide leadership and management of “VIBEs for Youth – Vision building, Identity, well-Being and Employability for Youth – Phase II” Project funded by Federal Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development (BMZ);

Job responsibilities
Provide leadership and management of “VIBEs for Youth – Vision building, Identity, well-Being and Employability for Youth – Phase II” Project funded by Federal Ministry of Economic Development (BMZ);
Implement project with due respect to donor requirements, SOS CVIs regulations and standard, national regulations, guidelines and local legislation;
With key project staff and stakeholders, ensure project strategic objectives and results are fully accomplished and meet donor requirements;
Maintain written track record of all project-related communication and agreements;
Keep all project-related documentation on file;
Organize project-related meetings.
Cooperate with state authorities, organizations and ensure their active participation in the project activities;
Implement project monitoring on national level, using data analysis as the basis for measuring performance;
Communicate on a regular basis with the project’s partner organization and report on the project’s progress;  
Supervise implementation, reporting and evaluation of the Project and oversee program on national level;
Review on regular basis project details, deliverables and schedules as per project Implementation Plan;
Produce final reports on time, in quality manner as per donor and SOS CVIs requirements;  
Lead Project Implementation team towards the achievements of project’s objectives with high quality standards;  
In line with SOS CVIs standards for leadership framework provide functional leadership for project staff;
Ensure close collaboration with the staff of programmes of SOS Children’s Villages Armenia and other colleagues to discuss issues facing the project, new ideas and achievements;
Support professional and personal development of staff.
Required qualifications
Advanced University degree in economics, management or social sciences 
At least 3-5 years of management experience, preferably on International projects;
Experience in finance, operations and team management; 
Experience of project/program concept development and management;
Practice in community development, consultation and partnership development;  
Excellent computer skills including Microsoft suite; 
Fluency in written and spoken English language.
Willingness to travel frequently.
Driving licence.


Competencies – knowledge, skills, abilities

Strong communication, presentation, facilitation and interpersonal skills; 
Ability to manage multiple tasks;  
Efficient task prioritization and time management; 
Flexibility to work both in team and independently;  
Work under time pressure;
Strategic, creative, and innovative thinking.
 
Required candidate level
C level
Professional Skills
Coordinating
Personal skills
Team management
