Job Description:

Support the Project Coordinator to manage  “VIBEs for Youth – Vision building, Identity, well-Being and Employability for Youth – Phase II” Project (financed by Federal Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development (BMZ)) budget, including tracking of financial and material resources;

Job responsibilities
Support the Project Coordinator to manage the project budget, including tracking of financial and material resources;
Ensure accurate and timely reporting of project finances and progress status;  
Implement project expenditure monitoring and review actual financial performance against the budget, and explain variances on a regular basis;
Ensure project staff compliance with all SOS CVI and SOS SV Armenia administrative and operational procedures and policies, as well as applicable donor regulations; 
Prepare project expenditures, budget adjustments, and cost modification requests to Project Director, SOS CV International, SOS Armenia and/or donor;
Maintain written track record of all project-related communication and agreements;
Keep all project-related documentation on file;
Review on regular basis project details, deliverables and schedules as project Implementation Plan;
Produce yearly and final reports on time, in quality manner as per donor requirements;  
Ensure the implementation of local Accounting standards and regulations, aligned with IFRS / IAS and local legislation.
Organise accounting system in a professional way, including: accounting software, documents management, and processes according to SOS CVI, SOS CV Armenia and donor’s requirements.  
Prepare correct annual budget to be incorporated into national planning and budgeting process.  
 
Required qualifications
University Degree in Accounting, Finance, Management, or another relevant field; 
At least 3 years of experience managing financial and contractual aspects of international development projects; 
Familiarity and experience with accounting programs and systems preferably with Finance Dynamic 365;
Experience of project/program concept development and management;
Demonstrated experience and skills in developing and managing project budgets;
Strong analytical and computer skills (applications and databases), with an emphasis on budget and financial analysis; 
Fluency in written and spoken English language.
Driving license
